1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:06,092
Discussing Energy Carefully At a symposium a speaker explained nuclear fission using

2
00:00:06,105 --> 00:00:12,829
a model reactor A uranium nucleus could split releasing energy The audience

3
00:00:12,842 --> 00:00:18,316
then compared this process with combustion in a fossil-fuel plant A refinery

4
00:00:18,447 --> 00:00:23,776
the speaker added served a different purpose from an electricity generator Mixing

5
00:00:23,789 --> 00:00:29,500
these concepts would produce a misleading debate Students asked about thermal efficiency

6
00:00:29,711 --> 00:00:35,553
carbon dioxide emission and the management of residual material No single number

7
00:00:35,566 --> 00:00:41,447
could express every consequence The speaker recommended a framework that considered cost

8
00:00:41,618 --> 00:00:48,145
reliability and environmental effects together A by-product that appeared negligible in one

9
00:00:48,158 --> 00:00:53,671
experiment might matter at a larger scale Before proposing a drastic change

10
00:00:53,908 --> 00:00:59,118
decision-makers should quantify the expected benefits and identify the assumptions behind them

11
00:01:00,026 --> 00:01:05,224
A balanced discussion requires neither blind enthusiasm nor blanket rejection but a

12
00:01:05,237 --> 00:01:07,342
clear account of the relevant evidence
